# Playback and downloads

`src/playback/` owns the player. Export a `PlayerEngine` (load album, play, pause, next, previous, seekBy ±10, skipTo, setRate, subscribe to status). V1 adapter: `react-native-nitro-player` `1.7.0-alpha.2` `TrackPlayer` + `PlayerQueue` with `repeat: 'off'`. Do not import `react-native-nitro-player` outside this folder. Do not add a second adapter in V1. Do not use nitro-player `DownloadManager`, Cast, or equalizer (Phase 5 stays `@kesha-antonov/react-native-background-downloader` + `react-native-notify-kit`).

Queue is a **single album**; playback **stops at the last track**. `loadAlbum` copies a **frozen session** (`albumId` + track `id`/`url`s) into one native playlist. Catalogue refresh updates Home/Library only — it must not rebuild the live queue. If the playing album or track is omitted from a new catalogue, keep playing the session until it ends. Native playlists are not the catalogue source of truth; prune extras on album load.

When a download finishes or files are removed, patch **upcoming** playlist URLs (`TrackPlayer.updateTracks`) while **pinning the current track’s URL** so the playing item is not restarted. **iOS never `updateTracks` a live 140+ item AVQueuePlayer** (main-thread hang). skip/end and `onTrackChange` (`reloadIfCurrentSourceStale`) resolve `file:` from disk (`withLocalUrls` / `playableUrlFor`). **Both platforms unpin on pause after the 2s audiobook rewind** (native paused listener: `applyPauseRewind` then `applyUpcomingSourceUpdates`). `engine.pause()` must not swap first — that set `skipPauseRewind` and skipped rewind. Paused current-URL change is `loadIntoNative` then pause; `skipPauseRewind` then ignores the synthetic pause. A complete **while already paused** must also notify the player so that swap runs (pause-listener only fires on the pause transition). **iOS live-queue notify is idle-only** (`!playing && !buffering`) so completes while playing do not queue the player mutex. Android still `updateTracks` while playing. **iOS `maxParallelDownloads` is always 1** (Android 3). While playing/buffering, never URLSession the current track or the next 3 (Nitro gapless window). Lock-while-playing (`AppState` `background` only) `start()`s leftover **unheld** rows into URLSession; held rows stay in the JS queue. Do not dump from Control Center / wifi-on (`inactive`) or NetInfo — that restore path after a kill native-crashed; wifi-on uses the JS pump (1-wide). Shade while playing or idle (no media session / JS suspended) posts **Downloading…** once, not a stuck done/total or percent; completed notices still post; pause with a live media session restores the count / percent. Toast `download.pausedWhilePlaying` only when leftover rows are all in that window. In-app next/prev/skipTo and ±10 overflow resolve `withLocalUrls()` first and reload at the target if its URL changed. Play / resume gates use `playableUrlFor`, not only `isLocalPlaybackUrl(track.url)`. Safety net: `onTrackChange` reloads that item if its frozen URL ≠ `playableUrlFor`. **iOS only:** native `end` mid-album is not album-end — AVQueuePlayer can empty when preloaded `https` next-items fail offline even if those files exist. Rebuild onto the next `file:` (or show `offlineStreamError` if it is not downloaded). Android `applyUpcomingSourceUpdates` syncs `nativeSourceUrls` after `updateTracks`. Downloads notify via `src/playback/live-queue.ts` (dynamic import — do not statically import playback from the download engine).

Resume **per album id** only:

```ts
{ [albumId]: { trackId: string; positionSec: number; updatedAt: number } }
```

History is a separate MMKV listen log (`src/state/history-store.ts`), not resume. Record when the current `albumId`+`trackId` changes (in-app, overflow, lock-screen skip). Pause/seek on the same track does not. Do not add a row if the newest entry is already that track (covers process death). The same track after a different one is a new row. Cap 50 events. `playedAt` is when that listen started (device timezone). If a track is playing or buffering, show Playing and open Now Playing; if paused mid-track, show resume time and play from per-album resume when `trackId` matches; ended/start-of-track and older rows play from 0.

Playback rate is **per album**, `0.25`–`2.0` in `0.25` steps, default `1.0`. Persist separately from resume position. `loadAlbum` applies that album’s saved rate. Do **not** add a Now Playing rate control in V1 (`setRate` + MMKV already exist). iOS lock-screen rate buttons are `0.5, 1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75, 2.0` (no `0.25` / `0.75`). Android has no rate media button.

Configure once: `showInNotification: true`, `carPlayEnabled` / `androidAutoEnabled` false, `remoteSkipForwardInterval` / `remoteSkipBackwardInterval` `10`. `PlayerConfig` has no extra flags — JS packs `icon:notification_icon`, `skipOnError`, `remotePrimary`, and `httpOverflow` into `androidNotificationIcon`. Native `applyConfigToken` sets Android `notificationSmallIconResName` from `icon:` (drawable `notification_icon`, copied at prebuild by `plugins/with-android-notification-icon.js`). `httpOverflow:1` (online) lets ±10 leftover land on an `https` neighbour; `httpOverflow:0` (offline) clamps if the neighbour URL is still `http(s)` and still overflows onto `file:`. JS `subscribeNetwork` reconfigures when online flips. Default native `allowHttpOverflow` is true. Lock screen / notification / Bluetooth Now Playing come from the native media session. Expanded Android shade tap uses session activity (`SessionActivityTrampoline` → `gurbaniaudioplayer://now-playing`). Compact shade and lock-screen controls are System UI and often will not open Now Playing. Needs a native Android build. In-app always shows both prev/next and ±10.

**Remote primary** (Settings, default ±10 / `"seek"`): compact notification, lock screen, Bluetooth, and car follow this pair. The other pair is **secondary** — in-app plus Android expanded notification overflow. `setRemotePrimary("seek" | "skip")` reconfigures native. Headset prev/next (`SEEK_TO_PREVIOUS` / `NEXT`, iOS `previousTrack`/`nextTrack`) follow primary. When primary is ±10, Android overflow prev/next are custom session commands so hardware can seek without also remapping expanded skip. Media3 disables `SEEK_TO_NEXT` on the last item — the `ForwardingPlayer` **adds** that command (and seek-forward) when primary is seek so Bluetooth +10 still works mid last-track. Do not strip commands or wrap session listeners (that dropped the notification). iOS Control Center shows numbered ±10 when primary is seek **and** keeps next/prev enabled so headset/car next-prev still seek ±10. When primary is skip, numbered buttons are hidden and next/prev skip tracks.

Lock screen / notification Previous still uses the library default when primary is track skip (~2s into the track restarts it; earlier than that goes to the previous track; first track restarts at 0). In-app prev uses the same ~2s restart so a `file:`/`https` mix does not skip via `skipToResolvedIndex`. Android System UI would otherwise call ExoPlayer `seekToPrevious` on a windowed timeline — the patch routes `SEEK_TO_PREVIOUS` / `NEXT` through `skipToPreviousOnQueue` / `skipToNextOnQueue` when primary is skip, and through overflowing ±10 when primary is seek. ±10 overflow at track boundaries is the same patch (`seekBackOverflowing` / `seekForwardOverflowing`, iOS `seekByOnQueue`): leftover time lands on the prev/next track while online (stream or `file:`); **offline**, leftover onto a still-`https` neighbour **clamps** (in-app `seekByOverflowing` and native `httpOverflow:0`); first-track −10 stays at 0; last-track +10 stays at the end. Do not override `getAvailableCommands` or wrap MediaSession player listeners (that dropped the notification). Next on the last track may still show; tapping it is a no-op because skip-next uses the logical album queue. `updateTracks` also skipped the current track unless the URL was empty — the same patch allows same-URL title/artist refresh on language change. Remote skip / headset prev persist resume from **fresh native state** (track change first, then MMKV). Do not flush the previous track.

User pause rewinds `PAUSE_REWIND_SEC` (2) and persists that position so resume orients the listener. Clamp at 0; do not overflow to the previous track. Applies to in-app, lock screen, sleep timer, and Bluetooth pause. Do **not** rewind when the track or album has ended (`reason === "end"` / native `stopped`) — that looped the last track.

Now Playing calls the engine, not nitro-player APIs: prev, next, −10s, play/pause, +10s. Second row: sleep timer, add bookmark, bookmarks, read along (`https://sttm.co/{currenScripture.sttmCoSlug}/{currentTrack.startAng}`). Hide read along if the current track has no `startAng` or the current scripture has no `sttmCoSlug`. Add bookmark opens `/now-playing/bookmark-note` (optional note) before saving. Album screens open that album’s bookmarks even when nothing is playing (`/a/{albumId}/bookmarks` or `/album/{albumId}/bookmarks`). Tapping a bookmark loads that track and **plays**. History and Bookmarks mute undownloaded rows while offline; `playAlbum` returns `false` and those screens must not push Now Playing.

Sleep timer: end of this track, remaining tracks through end of album, after N tracks, or hours+minutes (no seconds). Pause via the engine. Hours+minutes uses a `setTimeout` to `deadlineAt` (the 1s interval is only the remaining-time label). Note: Track/album timer options use `durationSec` on recorded tracks (`sehaj_paath`, `audiobook`). `radio` has live tracks, which have no duration — hide those options for live tracks.

Play errors: surface `PlayerStatus.error` on Now Playing in a reserved two-line slot (`PlaybackStatusLine` — layout must not jump). Mini player shows an error icon (`error-outline`) or buffering icon (`hourglass-empty`) next to the title — do not add that two-line slot there. Tap play to retry. Do not auto-play on foreground restore after an error or after the album ends. Native skip-on-source-error is **off** by default; `setSkipOnSourceError(true)` re-enables the library’s skip-to-next. Android leaves ExoPlayer’s `playerError` and sends Media3 `SessionError` (code name only — no app copy) so the shade/lock screen can show a failed state. iOS lock screen has no error slot; pause + play-to-retry is the signal. Buffering uses `PlayerStatus.buffering`. Keep-awake stays on while playing **or** buffering. Do not add `expo-keep-awake` to `app.json` plugins (it has no config plugin; Expo would load RN `index.js` and Metro would fail).

Interruptions (calls, maps, notifications): use the library’s native audio-focus / `AVAudioSession` defaults. Pause for a call, auto-resume when the system says `shouldResume` / focus returns. Do not JS-pause on those events (that would look like a user pause and block auto-resume). Ducking (maps, some alerts) stays ducked. Headphone unplug stays paused. Do not add a keep-alive hack.

Android `NitroPlayerPlaybackService` must stay a `mediaPlayback` FGS while `playWhenReady` and buffering or ready — not only while `isPlaying()`. Notification-icon refresh must not `stopForeground`. **Recents swipe / Close all** always `pauseAllPlayersAndStopSelf()`(`onTaskRemoved`). Do not keep audio alive after the user dismisses the task. After pause / end / error, Media3’s 10-minute FGS timeout still applies. Settings **Unrestricted battery** (Android only) opens system app settings so OEM battery saving (OnePlus Hans and similar) does not freeze a background stream. Needs a new native Android build.


Downloads and Offline mode

Downloads: `@kesha-antonov/react-native-background-downloader` (`skipMmkvDependency: true` with MMKV). Settings **Download on Wi-Fi only** (default on). When on, refuse cellular and point to Settings; when off, warn before downloading on mobile network. Batch album or per track; re-attach after process death. `react-native-notify-kit`: One progress notification per batch album download; separate notifications for individual track downloads. Prefer local file if present, else stream (live queue: upcoming items only; do not swap the currently playing source). Index by `trackId` + URL. Do not cancel an in-flight download because a catalogue refresh omitted that track; finish it and mark **orphan** if `trackId` is absent from the live catalogue and not in the current session. Prune orphans only when they are not playing and not downloading.  After reinstall, give user option to restore the cloud **wanted-offline** id list to re-download.

Detect internet and show a peristent offline banner when the network is gone (without overlapping app content). Debounce going offline by 3 seconds (`lodash/debounce` in `src/downloads/network.ts`); apply online immediately so a brief drop does not pause a stream. Do not JS-pause a healthy stream on NetInfo — keep playing from the native buffer (same as background / lock screen). When native buffers or errors on a CDN track while offline, show `offlineStreamError` and stop. Play stays disabled on an undownloaded stream while offline; tap play to retry after reconnect. Local files keep playing.
When a track is about to play, prefer the local file if it exists; if an in-queue offline file was deleted outside the app, fallback to online version without crashing. Other in-queue downloads can be removed and the live queue switches those items back to stream. The player engine still has to handle files removed by the user or OS.
Online functions should be disabled when app goes offline: unsaved tracks should be muted (disabled) and should not start streaming, read along button (external link) should be disabled. Show a downloaded icon in each track entry if so. Show a downloaded icon on the collection list if all tracks are downloaded. Add a multi-select track option (with select all) to select tracks for download. Download all(/remove all) option should also be provided. Phone memory should be checked before downloading if it is enough (sum catalogue `byteSize`; 50 MB margin). If not user should be notified. App UI must not delete the **currently playing or buffering** file (`isCurrentlyPlayingTrack`); paused current-file delete is OK if resume can fall back to stream when online. Restored download jobs whose dest already matches `byteSize` must mark complete and free the pump **without** `stop()` on a still-DOWNLOADING/PENDING native job (`stop()` deletes the dest). `sweepIdleNativeJobs` must not `stop()` those running jobs either.


Car V1: lock screen / notification / Bluetooth Now Playing from the adapter. Car browse/queue is later (not V1).
